%I A397095 #43 Oct 02 2026 22:51:26
%S A397095 2,7,23,59,227,401,71,3643,62939,480209,292627,1089427,48773651,
%T A397095 2374649
%N A397095 a(n) is the smallest prime dividing exactly n numbers of the form k! + 1 (k > 0).
%C A397095 a(n) >= A230315(n).
%C A397095 According to A230315, a(15) > a(16) = 584133523.
%H A397095 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilson%27s_theorem">Wilson's theorem</a>.
%e A397095 227 divides 61!+1, 113!+1, 144!+1, 165!+1, 226!+1. No prime less than 227 has 5 solutions, so a(5) = 227.
%t A397095 m=100;Table[SelectFirst[Table[{p,Select[Range[p-1],Mod[#!+1,p]==0&]},{p,Prime[Range[m]]}],Length[#[[2]]]==n&],{n,7}][[All,1]]
%Y A397095 Cf. A051301, A230315.
%K A397095 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A397095 1,1
%A A397095 _Zhining Yang_, Aug 20 2026
